\title{Smoothed and projected quantities from a fit}
\description{
Built by \link{GCFit}\verb{$project()}. Inside the observation window these are
\emph{smoothed} -- every survey in the deme, later ones included, informs the
state at each step -- and beyond the last survey they are projections from
the same kernel, started from the smoothed lattice distribution at the
last step.

\code{p_present} can nevertheless step at the join, and the step can be large.
A survey at the final step is a hard constraint that the smoother obeys
and the projection does not: a deme seen positive there has
\code{p_present = 1} at \code{T} and less immediately after, because extinction
becomes possible again. A deme carrying mass at zero jumps the other way,
since a fraction \code{1 - exp(-lambda)} of that mass -- a quarter to a third
at the fitted influx -- arrives in a single step. On the Ugandan panel
the jump runs from -0.13 to +0.09. It is a property of the model, not an
artefact of stitching two calculations together: the lattice distribution
itself is propagated continuously.
}
\section{Two kinds of interval}{

\verb{f_q*} are posterior predictive quantiles of the latent frequency:
\code{theta}, the latent path and the Wright-Fisher noise are all integrated
out, so \code{f_q97.5} is a predictive bound on the frequency itself.
\verb{p_present_q*} are quantiles of \code{P(present | X, theta)} \strong{across draws}:
everything but \code{theta} is integrated out, so they say how well the data
pin a probability, not how uncertain the outcome is. Presence is a
Bernoulli whose probability is itself uncertain, and
\code{Var(1) = E[p(1-p)] + Var(p)}; the \verb{p_present_q*} columns show only the
second term.
}

\section{What is unconditional}{

The \verb{f_*} columns carry the atom at zero: it has mass
\code{1 - p_present}, so any quantile below that level is exactly \code{0}, and a
band resting on zero means absence is the likelier state rather than a
frequency near zero.
}

\section{The two introduction-time columns}{

Under \code{founding = "rate"} the first presence time is no longer \verb{t*}:
the deme joins the flow process at \verb{t*} and may sit empty for a while, so
\code{pmf_tfirst} is the posterior for \verb{t*} and \code{T_first} from sampled paths
is a later, separate quantity.

\code{pmf_tfirst} is free and exact. In this model the founding event deposits
a copy at \verb{t*} and nothing is present before it, so the first presence
time \emph{is} \verb{t*}, which the likelihood already marginalises analytically.
\code{pmf_test} is a path functional -- no marginal of the smoother says when
the excursion carrying the first detected copy began -- so it needs
\code{n_paths > 0} and is \code{NA} otherwise. Walk back from the first survey with
a non-zero count until the deme is empty: that is where the lineage which
was actually seen began. It is a proper distribution in a deme that was
detected and absent in one that was not, there being no observed lineage
to date, and it does not condition on survival -- the lineage that was
seen need not be the one still present at \code{T}. It is bounded above by the
detection that defines it and below by \verb{t*}.
Both are zero on projected rows, not \code{NA}: \verb{t*} is supported on \verb{1..T}
only, and that is the documented limitation of this model rather than
missing information.
}

